#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124470 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124277 :question/id #uuid "033e459e-5148-5e78-ab5c-7e455b06cd64" :question/math-academy-id "e-3695" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z) = xz\\ln{y}$ and $\\mathbf r (t) =  t^2 \\, \\mathbf i + t  \\, \\mathbf j +t^3  \\, \\mathbf k,$ compute $\\dfrac {\\textrm d}{\\textrm d t} [f(\\mathbf r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm d}{\\textrm d t} [f(\\mathbf r (t))] = \\nabla f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf r'(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\nabla f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,k \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,i+\\frac{xz}{y}\\,j+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x= t^2,$ $y = t$ and $z= t^3$ into the above to find $\\nabla f(\\mathbf{r}(t)){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & ={t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{4}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =({t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{4}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (2t\\,i+\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k) \\\\  & =({t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\cdot 2t+({t}^{4})\\cdot 1+({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+{t}^{4}+3{t}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & ={t}^{4}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "112e3378-bde8-5896-822e-e815bde51501" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556007 :question-generator/id #uuid "10ad4d6c-c271-5873-87a1-cccc6bed0a8f" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124470.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6b5248-8092-5223-a861-76c990d98151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t+1}+(1+2t){e}^{t}+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445647} {:answer/id #uuid "3f8c2a6a-498f-5431-bf0a-f09364aeca5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}+2e+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445649} {:answer/id #uuid "55795f5b-54c2-5a78-8f3f-d7bc330a0c55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t+1}+(t+1){e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445653} {:answer/id #uuid "88d607c8-fe3c-5a8f-95e2-26b4560aaab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t+1}+(1+t){e}^{t}+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445659} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2dcd24-b4f5-5abd-afe6-bb8c91b06230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t+1}+t{e}^{t}+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d607c8-fe3c-5a8f-95e2-26b4560aaab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t+1}+(1+t){e}^{t}+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445659} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f9b55f-9f7a-5171-8a0f-7462d539b472" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f10e177e-2926-5cde-8e9a-4b0a99b2ff4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36238" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+e\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+yz+xz)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+yz+xz)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy+yz+xz)\\,k \\\\  & =(y+z)\\,i+(x+z)\\,j+(y+x)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y={e}^{t},$ and $z=e$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =({e}^{t}+e)\\,i+(t+e)\\,j+({e}^{t}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e)\\,k \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t}\\,j+(0)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(({e}^{t}+e)\\,i+(t+e)\\,j+({e}^{t}+t)\\,k)\\cdot (i+{e}^{t}\\,j+(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+e)\\cdot 1+(t+e)\\cdot {e}^{t}+({e}^{t}+t)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+e+t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t+1} \\\\  & ={e}^{t+1}+(1+t){e}^{t}+e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f80eba8-e277-54b6-a822-397fce4bd264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124103} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab97f80-a525-5bbe-a6b4-4f61835de51f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479565} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4d169e-765b-5d10-9ef3-ea60b0437938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479620} {:answer/id #uuid "e711ca65-092d-53a1-9492-fad3c11a523c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479701} {:answer/id #uuid "eef6c2ca-b384-52f9-bf10-2db701968ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eef6c2ca-b384-52f9-bf10-2db701968ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479712} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d53ae6-99b0-5b9a-984f-d8cbdd57249f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9127ceaf-3e13-50a4-b08a-89114324036d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95075" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=z(x+y)$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z(x+y))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z(x+y))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z(x+y))\\,k \\\\  & =z\\,i+z\\,j+(x+y)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & ={e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =({e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1346c66e-add9-58bb-914d-bde230ffb97c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281874} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbc6691-be3c-5174-bc33-891dad11a619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282476} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca6cbe6-66c9-5cdf-85f9-16bcc6c8db5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282765} {:answer/id #uuid "c8135d32-63d4-5f0e-ba7b-566e64774dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283438} {:answer/id #uuid "d748975e-258c-5fd7-a8c3-a751942b65a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ca6cbe6-66c9-5cdf-85f9-16bcc6c8db5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282765} :answer-field/id #uuid "771db56a-a84d-5c67-ab37-e76a138f7e66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78b6efe3-1fb5-5655-97e2-03def53db36e" :question/math-academy-id "q-167453" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{3}$ and $r(t)={t}^{3}\\,i+\\,j+t\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{3})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\,i+(2xy+{z}^{3})\\,j+3y{z}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{3},y=1,$ and $z=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\,i+3{t}^{3}\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}i+(0)\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\,i+3{t}^{3}\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}i+(0)\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}\\cdot 0+3{t}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043ac664-b524-524e-aa72-bf1d30123527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357793} {:answer/id #uuid "af3ddaa4-8953-5d46-9032-e2f95ff616b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t{cos}^{3}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359275} {:answer/id #uuid "c43dfc74-6743-5922-a14e-6c2caaeb73de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{3}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359473} {:answer/id #uuid "cc97c0a8-0127-5bdc-a492-17ba4f68be95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359546} {:answer/id #uuid "da9c33c8-b2a5-5f98-b17d-5810e16dbeda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "043ac664-b524-524e-aa72-bf1d30123527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357793} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9feea77-0770-57d9-9bdc-bf443c95c674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a60dcabe-5a9f-584e-9268-2f3213ceda5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95070" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{4}-{y}^{4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\,i-4{y}^{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $z=2t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,i-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,i-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{cos}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1347f5a2-01c0-5c7b-b717-680930abc12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t{e}^{t}+1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357914} {:answer/id #uuid "4c03b829-963e-5a53-bccb-1865320c6ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}+1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358409} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8b2be7-935d-58f9-a8d2-f58e5e602a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t-1}(1-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358993} {:answer/id #uuid "a48fbdf1-c888-5cc7-ad1f-26a035cc7e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t+1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359180} {:answer/id #uuid "aa082587-0924-59bd-be2d-48ce5c0b988c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a48fbdf1-c888-5cc7-ad1f-26a035cc7e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t+1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359180} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6ee750-c6b9-5399-bdf4-e7500571e2b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75389de5-3518-524a-bf8a-ad60601e753c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95072" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{yz}{xyz}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{xyz}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{xyz}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,j+\\frac{1}{z}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y={e}^{t-1},$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t-1}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t-1}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\,k)\\cdot (i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{{e}^{t-1}}{{e}^{t-1}}+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d173fc-2ace-5c23-8e6c-2e1100a8bcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t(t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358124} {:answer/id #uuid "55409a0b-0c25-504a-bd65-c0781332f04d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+4t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358492} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0052e5-1ee4-5d5c-9667-77f78de9d0a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359564} {:answer/id #uuid "ee064399-1401-555f-b6c0-3013abc3be94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359872} {:answer/id #uuid "f41185b3-09b1-59b6-88eb-3c7555fb8f88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f41185b3-09b1-59b6-88eb-3c7555fb8f88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359919} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6daa545-65f3-5e47-b745-8aab21ef0ff5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce5cc103-892b-5471-8317-cbb325d2454d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95142" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+(t+1)\\,j+(t-1)\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}[x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})]\\,k \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,i+2xy\\,j-2xz\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ $y=t+1$ and $z=t-1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =[(t+1)^{2}-(t-1)^{2}]i+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot (t+1)\\,j-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot (t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =4t\\,i+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(4t\\,i+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =4t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot 1-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4+2(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2(t-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67fb2e01-985f-513d-813b-cfde3f1b377e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358661} {:answer/id #uuid "788c776c-5597-51d2-9394-be9dfb7f75ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358792} {:answer/id #uuid "901c96ff-6cee-55e9-8211-cd0101addfb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359007} {:answer/id #uuid "a22be918-009f-5e59-9d70-9b6808c8792a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359167} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc10872-0c59-572a-92f2-5c00d7f80870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbc10872-0c59-572a-92f2-5c00d7f80870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359542} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef695bf-af69-5590-8e72-7ce89ea59101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee940918-1cef-5c23-a56c-5afe1494fd57" :question/math-academy-id "q-95146" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,k \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={t}^{2},y={e}^{t},$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (2t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{t}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}+2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5305687e-83d8-5c87-af7d-a5b0a362d788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+{e}^{{t}^{2}}+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358466} {:answer/id #uuid "631de459-4352-5ad1-949e-8ac23d4b20f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358613} {:answer/id #uuid "b15809fa-40bc-5563-9a51-d40e84efc938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359292} {:answer/id #uuid "c66b80bb-3662-52ab-bf2e-dab3fb4673d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{e}^{{t}^{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359496} {:answer/id #uuid "e0073e63-c4b1-5f0a-b806-ed90e183c49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\frac{{e}^{{t}^{2}}}{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15809fa-40bc-5563-9a51-d40e84efc938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359292} :answer-field/id #uuid "d86a4006-7e81-5ee9-a91c-4ead86d71714" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "312e3468-92a5-5996-9fc8-ac654be83975" :question/math-academy-id "q-95149" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y}$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+{e}^{y}\\,j+\\frac{1}{z}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,y={t}^{2},$ and $z=\\frac{1}{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\,j+t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\,j+t\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a36a033-d9b0-5aa7-a7f4-b5451390ac7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445648} {:answer/id #uuid "60dab585-b4f4-59ea-8d98-9a5182b158eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445654} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6d49e7-278c-5501-995f-670dd3f19484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+2t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445660} {:answer/id #uuid "d82ae990-52e1-5862-b9ec-b3ce7c4bd555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445667} {:answer/id #uuid "ff848b94-7fca-53f6-95e5-3ab48c4f01c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d82ae990-52e1-5862-b9ec-b3ce7c4bd555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445667} :answer-field/id #uuid "88e49b12-6312-563d-bb5a-a9112af44abf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "430b6986-f30c-500a-b5e9-219dd0f3ace5" :question/math-academy-id "q-167463" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+2t\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))\\,k \\\\  & =yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\,i+xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\,j+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,$ $y=2t$ and $z=\\frac{1}{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,k)\\cdot (\\,i+2\\,j-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\cdot 2+2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a16002-fb70-57d8-b56c-e846ae55b5f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479469} {:answer/id #uuid "800531bb-e5bf-57d0-94df-bfb46de70ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479550} {:answer/id #uuid "87ac30df-06f9-515c-b483-8fa371168b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({t}^{2}-1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479560} {:answer/id #uuid "c3353af3-19ba-5e14-a733-a22abed74ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479654} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa24879-c05e-53a3-b066-9afb3802f261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3353af3-19ba-5e14-a733-a22abed74ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479654} :answer-field/id #uuid "65e8ce36-6bdd-5ffc-86d9-2cca52842880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23fc0071-5d5d-57b9-949a-5e0f696a08ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-95074" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$ and $r(t)=(t+1)\\,i+(t-1)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =2x\\,i+2y\\,j+4z\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t+1,$ $y=t-1$ and $z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =2(t+1)\\,i+2(t-1)\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =i+j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(2(t+1)\\,i+2(t-1)\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (i+j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =2(t+1)\\cdot 1+2(t-1)\\cdot 1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2t+2+2t-2+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =4(t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a625792-3ebb-5931-8a2d-6a88c5f87ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479401} {:answer/id #uuid "2f3fec76-0a6e-5e27-983b-461d88932bfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479430} {:answer/id #uuid "a28056a9-f916-52a5-9c57-bf67a29a290d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479603} {:answer/id #uuid "b34fbe3e-3237-5a50-aaa6-a8cad66ce7ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479626} {:answer/id #uuid "bce18e25-d9a2-5b97-b848-b56b779ae552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce18e25-d9a2-5b97-b848-b56b779ae552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479644} :answer-field/id #uuid "73405ecf-58c2-52c0-a13d-a399aaa1b75c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f5e2cc69-b41b-55a6-ba1d-f0aa44f4db50" :question/math-academy-id "q-95143" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,i-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,j+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,i-\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,j+\\operatorname{cot}⁡z\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,$ $y={t}^{2}$ and $z={e}^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}\\,j+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}\\,k)\\cdot (i+2t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{tan}⁡{t}^{2}+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "131e1312-3232-541a-a772-9a4195876e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484854} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf61e8f-1cbe-5cf7-b7de-cb285c2945df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484868} {:answer/id #uuid "54a8785f-b684-5fbf-ab5e-7a2651308e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485006} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1155ed-ffcf-5482-9835-4e132b93d976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485086} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4e5d76-01d4-5027-9d0b-5f4455a3c94c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54a8785f-b684-5fbf-ab5e-7a2651308e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485006} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f9db34-f1fa-54a6-9839-7f297b6a756c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eabe5e6a-dc85-5118-84d2-9aa9f31a6a23" :question/math-academy-id "q-95086" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)$ and $r(t)=(t+1)\\,i+2t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t+1,$ $y=2t$ and $z={t}^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,k)\\cdot (\\,i+2\\,j+2t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 1+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 2+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2t(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)(1+t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "326ed290-c2d9-50d2-88c8-74db06917de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t \\left(t + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555967} {:answer/id #uuid "336c3865-f674-544a-82cb-712e32c64648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (6 t + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555969} {:answer/id #uuid "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2 t + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555973} {:answer/id #uuid "56a00959-2111-50b5-b5fe-ba2f85d7c3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555977} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e4f8f2-4f25-544c-a9ba-33e2472e1343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2 t + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555973} :answer-field/id #uuid "32e468ca-2d16-55b6-a084-1a0ff8b6f7f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11cc55a9-a3be-504c-b916-0f019947db61" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=- x - 3 y + 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (1)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t)+(2)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(-1)+(- 6 t)+(4 t) \\\\  & =- (2 t + 1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f8edcc7-83f3-51eb-a02a-f98f35085a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 10 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555966} {:answer/id #uuid "69f314a2-61a8-53f2-b0ac-eb90c1a11c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (10 t + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555981} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0b14be-60a6-545a-ac09-803a1de56af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555986} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad1d7fe-61c1-5328-9f74-34705da6c672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (4 t + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555987} {:answer/id #uuid "99bcbeaa-ab4e-516c-bbf9-8ff846ba257b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t \\left(5 t + 3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69f314a2-61a8-53f2-b0ac-eb90c1a11c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (10 t + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555981} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c278396-ed1e-50e5-a1d5-838e5e5875f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "216d3edd-79b6-5b78-9d7a-c69bb1f635e7" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-3)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k) \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (1)+(-2)\\cdot (2 t)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(-3)+(- 4 t)+(- 6 t) \\\\  & =- (10 t + 3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a17b40b-479d-5751-b0e3-83bf67df5a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t \\left(3 t + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555972} {:answer/id #uuid "6377a370-44ec-5cec-9bc0-51c381fef7ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555980} {:answer/id #uuid "72871cc2-889b-515a-9b90-c36e695dffa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\left(3 t + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555984} {:answer/id #uuid "7f26a776-36f8-56ac-8203-f0bde320ccfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (6 t + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555988} {:answer/id #uuid "e493d7f7-de85-5a7d-9fa4-d1fef1c84e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - 6 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f26a776-36f8-56ac-8203-f0bde320ccfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (6 t + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555988} :answer-field/id #uuid "083c6ee8-7fc2-50bc-af5d-3d6b19fae25c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ed8bb8a-ea3c-5edb-81c1-5b691ab3509b" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x - 3 y - 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t)\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x - 3 y - 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x - 3 y - 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x - 3 y - 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(-2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot (1)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t)+(-2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1)+(- 6 t)+(-2) \\\\  & =- (6 t + 1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce4be0f-5d33-51bc-9050-760037179d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{2} e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555963} {:answer/id #uuid "357d82b0-b468-5bc5-b46c-2ef6c8defaa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\left(- t \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}\\right) e^{2} e^{2 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555970} {:answer/id #uuid "55240750-0f78-5bc6-92b3-9cedb81aed12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}\\right) e^{2} e^{2 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555976} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4a2f77-851b-5117-b328-24f12ba3ba72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 e^{2} e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555979} {:answer/id #uuid "97ca2dc3-593b-53d0-842f-e141944c8015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e \\left(- e e^{t} \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}\\right) e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "357d82b0-b468-5bc5-b46c-2ef6c8defaa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\left(- t \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t^{2} + 2 t + 1 \\right)}\\right) e^{2} e^{2 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555970} :answer-field/id #uuid "7227fc03-6c4a-59f2-afbf-1702442c4391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8f25a065-b9d2-5631-91bf-0e1b3f75fc51" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right)$ and $r(t)={(t + 1)}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\,j+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,k \\\\  & =(4\\left(-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={(t + 1)}^{2},y={e}^{(t + 1)},$ and $z={e}^{(t + 1)}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(4\\left(-{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({(t + 1)}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k \\\\  & =(2(t + 1))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((4\\left(-{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,k)\\cdot ((2(t + 1))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\left(-2(t + 1){e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t + 1)}+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t + 1)}\\right) \\\\  & =4\\left(-2(t + 1){e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})+2{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right) \\\\  & =4\\left(2{e}^{2(t + 1)}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})-(t + 1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2}))\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d1d6bd-d89b-5bad-bd17-b50341f803cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(2 - t\\right) e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}}{e^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555960} {:answer/id #uuid "4664a78f-effb-5ddf-988f-356dddd95a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}}{e^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555971} {:answer/id #uuid "8f66985e-58fb-59d3-98c8-1287b1ccd811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(- t \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}\\right) e^{2 t}}{e^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555991} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f54656-e29a-5b5b-890b-fac4665b8674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(- \\frac{e^{t} \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}}{e^{2}} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555997} {:answer/id #uuid "ee89e640-8825-5ae1-b367-7b5359189bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}\\right) e^{2 t}}{e^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f66985e-58fb-59d3-98c8-1287b1ccd811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(- t \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t^{2} - 4 t + 4 \\right)}\\right) e^{2 t}}{e^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555991} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7f1241-2ff1-5381-8dd4-2f497ed46b35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b766d452-c3b3-5624-a6b9-7ef01ce70700" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $r(t)={(t - 2)}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\,j+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,k \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={(t - 2)}^{2},y={e}^{(t - 2)},$ and $z={e}^{(t - 2)}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(-{e}^{2(t - 2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,j+(+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({(t - 2)}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t - 2)})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t - 2)})\\,k \\\\  & =(2(t - 2))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t - 2)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t - 2)})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-{e}^{2(t - 2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,j+(+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))\\,k)\\cdot ((2(t - 2))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t - 2)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t - 2)})\\,k) \\\\  & =-2(t - 2){e}^{2(t - 2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t - 2)}+{e}^{(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t - 2)} \\\\  & =-2(t - 2){e}^{2(t - 2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})+2{e}^{2(t - 2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2(t - 2)}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})-(t - 2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c54f7b-0460-5650-8e11-7dbfff0c05e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555958} {:answer/id #uuid "6add913c-9635-5380-9dd3-082d19b4c8e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(1 - 3 t\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555982} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a53ab2-3b2d-511f-8d27-0c2e3593b2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555995} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0ce4fb-faf2-545c-813c-92335b2551d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t \\left(2 - t\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556000} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d2ded-87cd-520a-9927-cc57f85daf7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(1 - t\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d2ded-87cd-520a-9927-cc57f85daf7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(1 - t\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556001} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea5389a-261a-518e-b827-bc0fb8107846" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b831457d-f088-5348-bc3d-27f5556d6376" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=2 x - 3 y + 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2 x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(2)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((2)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2)\\cdot (1)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t)+(2)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(2)+(- 6 t)+(4 t) \\\\  & =2 \\left(1 - t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555959} {:answer/id #uuid "09f295d9-03a2-5561-bbef-04c9bb89034c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555962} {:answer/id #uuid "78c86cc8-66c7-50dd-9fc4-ded5ae059599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555985} {:answer/id #uuid "d334b550-3042-553b-b847-e1e7fe52d626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(t - 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556002} {:answer/id #uuid "d9187c94-57be-571f-b824-8290c0c50c00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t \\left(t - 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555959} :answer-field/id #uuid "844dfb74-8a60-5fe0-bb44-50294978c57a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbb4e13f-d8a8-5c5d-b9d1-448311f2dde4" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x + y - 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t)\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x + y - 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x + y - 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x + y - 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot (1)+(1)\\cdot (2 t)+(-2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1)+(2 t)+(-2) \\\\  & =2 t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Form of the Chain Rule to a Function of Three Variables"}]}
